      `I intend to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to use it, or to cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property?
      `what the thing is` IS A `What the thing is` @desc What best describes the thing you intended to be destroyed or damaged?
      `I have custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have custody or control of it?
      `what interest I have in it` IS A `Interest in property` @desc What interest, if any, do you have in it? An interest that is only equitable and arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest is a separate choice.
      `I have a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a charge on it?
      `I have a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you enforce a trust to which it is subject?
      `I am the corporation sole whose property it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation sole (an office-holder that is a legal person in its own right, such as a bishop) whose property it is, whether or not the office is vacant?
      `the person who would use it has custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who would use it (or cause it to be used) have custody or control of it?
      `what interest the person who would use it has in it` IS A `Interest in property` @desc What interest, if any, does the person who would use it (or cause it to be used) have in it? An interest that is only equitable and arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest is a separate choice.
      `the person who would use it has a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who would use it (or cause it to be used) have a charge on it?
      `the person who would use it has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the person who would use it (or cause it to be used) enforce a trust to which it is subject?
      `the person who would use it is the corporation sole whose property it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who would use it (or cause it to be used) the corporation sole (an office-holder that is a legal person in its own right, such as a bishop) whose property it is, whether or not the office is vacant?
      `I intended it to be destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend it to be destroyed or damaged?
      `I intended that only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that to happen only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains?
      `the intended change would impair the physical condition of the computer or storage medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that change impair the physical condition of the computer or storage medium?
      `I knew it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know it was likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person?
      `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any other lawful excuse or defence recognised by law, apart from section 5(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence under section 3(b)` IS
    `a person commits an offence under section 3(b)` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my connection` MEANS Connection WITH
            `custody or control of it` IS `I have custody or control of it`
            `interest in it` IS `what interest I have in it`
            `a charge on it` IS `I have a charge on it`
            `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS `I have a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
            `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS `I am the corporation sole whose property it is`
        
        `the user's connection` MEANS Connection WITH
            `custody or control of it` IS `the person who would use it has custody or control of it`
            `interest in it` IS `what interest the person who would use it has in it`
            `a charge on it` IS `the person who would use it has a charge on it`
            `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS `the person who would use it has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
            `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS `the person who would use it is the corporation sole whose property it is`
        
        `my property` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
            `the thing` IS `the thing described by` `what the thing is`
            `the accused's connection with it` IS `my connection`
            `other persons' connections with it` IS EMPTY  -- not asked: this rule does not read it
        
        `my damage` MEANS Damage WITH
            `destruction or damage` IS `I intended it to be destroyed or damaged`
            `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS `I intended that only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains`
            `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS `the intended change would impair the physical condition of the computer or storage medium`
        
        `my lawful excuse` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
            `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS `a belief not asked about`  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS `a belief not asked about`  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS FALSE  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS FALSE  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS FALSE  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS FALSE  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `a belief not asked about`  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS `a belief not asked about`  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS `a belief not asked about`  -- not asked: section 5(2) does not apply to this offence, so this is never read
            `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law`
        
        `my case` MEANS `Section 3 facts` WITH
            `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS `I have something in my custody or under my control`
            `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS `I intend to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property`
            `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS `my property`
            `the intended damage` IS `my damage`
            `the user's connection with the property` IS `the user's connection`
            `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS `I knew it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person`
            `lawful excuse` IS `my lawful excuse`

§ `Section 4 -- Punishment of offences`

-- s 4(1), s 4(2). The CEILING the Act sets, not the sentence a court passes.
@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of this offence?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc Which offence is it?
      `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will you be, or were you, convicted?
GIVETH A `Maximum imprisonment`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of this offence` IS
    `the most that can follow` `how I am convicted` (LIST `the offence`)

-- s 4, applied to what the person did under section 1.
@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted on indictment of what I did under section 1?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `What the thing is` @desc What best describes the thing you destroyed or damaged?
      `someone else has custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does anyone other than you have custody or control of it?
      `what interest someone else has in it` IS A `Interest in property` @desc What interest, if any, does anyone other than you have in it? An interest that is only equitable and arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest is a separate choice.
      `someone else has a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does anyone other than you have a charge on it?
      `someone else has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can anyone other than you enforce a trust to which it is subject?
      `someone else is the corporation sole whose property it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone other than you the corporation sole (an office-holder that is a legal person in its own right, such as a bishop) whose property it is, whether or not the office is vacant?
      `I destroyed or damaged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you destroy or damage it?
      `I did so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains?
      `the change impaired the physical condition of the computer or storage medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that change impair the physical condition of the computer or storage medium?
      `the destruction or damage was by fire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the destruction or damage done by fire?
      `I intended to destroy or damage that property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to destroy or damage that property?
      `I was reckless as to whether that property would be destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether that property would be destroyed or damaged?
      `I intended to destroy or damage property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to destroy or damage property, whoever it belonged to?
      `I was reckless as to whether property would be destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether property, whoever it belonged to, would be destroyed or damaged?
      `I intended by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend, by the destruction or damage, to endanger the life of another?
      `I was reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether the life of another would be endangered by it?
      `I honestly believed those entitled to consent had consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the person or persons entitled to consent to the destruction or damage had consented to it?
      `I honestly believed those entitled to consent would have consented had they known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that they would have consented, had they known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances?
      `I acted to protect property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect property belonging to you or another?
      `I acted to protect a right or interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect a right or interest in property?
      `I acted to protect a right or privilege in or over land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise?
      `that right or interest was in fact vested in me or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the right or interest in fact vested in you or another?
      `I honestly believed that right or interest was vested in me or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe the right or interest was vested in you or another?
      `I honestly believed the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection?
      `I honestly believed the means of protection were reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the means of protection you adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable, having regard to all the circumstances?
      `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any other lawful excuse or defence recognised by law, apart from section 5(2)?
GIVETH A `Maximum imprisonment`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted on indictment of what I did under section 1` IS
    `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (`the offences committed under section 1` `my case`)
    WHERE
        `another person's connection` MEANS Connection WITH
            `custody or control of it` IS `someone else has custody or control of it`
            `interest in it` IS `what interest someone else has in it`
            `a charge on it` IS `someone else has a charge on it`
            `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS `someone else has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
            `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS `someone else is the corporation sole whose property it is`
        
        `my property` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
            `the thing` IS `the thing described by` `what the thing is`
            `the accused's connection with it` IS `a connection not asked about`  -- not asked: this rule does not read it
            `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `another person's connection`
        
        `my damage` MEANS Damage WITH
            `destruction or damage` IS `I destroyed or damaged it`
            `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS `I did so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains`
            `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS `the change impaired the physical condition of the computer or storage medium`
        
        `my lawful excuse` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
            `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed those entitled to consent had consented`
            `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed those entitled to consent would have consented had they known`
            `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS `I acted to protect property`
            `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS `I acted to protect a right or interest in property`
            `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS `I acted to protect a right or privilege in or over land`
            `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `that right or interest was in fact vested in me or another`
            `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed that right or interest was vested in me or another`
            `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection`
            `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed the means of protection were reasonable`
            `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law`
        
        `my case` MEANS `Section 1 facts` WITH
            `the property` IS `my property`
            `the damage` IS `my damage`
            `the destruction or damage was by fire` IS `the destruction or damage was by fire`
            `intending to destroy or damage any such property` IS `I intended to destroy or damage that property`
            `reckless as to whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged` IS `I was reckless as to whether that property would be destroyed or damaged`
            `intending to destroy or damage any property` IS `I intended to destroy or damage property`
            `reckless as to whether any property would be destroyed or damaged` IS `I was reckless as to whether property would be destroyed or damaged`
            `intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another` IS `I intended by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another`
            `reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered` IS `I was reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered`
            `lawful excuse` IS `my lawful excuse`

§ `Section 5 -- "Without lawful excuse"`

-- s 5(1). Section 5 deems a lawful excuse only for some limbs of sections 1 to 3.
@export Does section 5 apply to this offence?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc Which offence is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 5 apply to this offence` IS
    `section 5 applies to` `the offence`

-- s 5(2), (3), (5). Whether the person has a lawful excuse for the offence, from
-- the facts they state.
@export Do I have a lawful excuse for this offence?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc Which offence is it?
      `I honestly believed those entitled to consent had consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the person or persons entitled to consent to the destruction or damage had consented to it?
      `I honestly believed those entitled to consent would have consented had they known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that they would have consented, had they known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances?
      `I acted to protect property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect property belonging to you or another?
      `I acted to protect a right or interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect a right or interest in property?
      `I acted to protect a right or privilege in or over land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in order to protect a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise?
      `that right or interest was in fact vested in me or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the right or interest in fact vested in you or another?
      `I honestly believed that right or interest was vested in me or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe the right or interest was vested in you or another?
      `I honestly believed the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection?
      `I honestly believed the means of protection were reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe that the means of protection you adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable, having regard to all the circumstances?
      `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any other lawful excuse or defence recognised by law, apart from section 5(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a lawful excuse for this offence` IS
    `the accused has a lawful excuse for` `the offence` `my lawful excuse`
    WHERE
        `my lawful excuse` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
            `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed those entitled to consent had consented`
            `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed those entitled to consent would have consented had they known`
            `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS `I acted to protect property`
            `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS `I acted to protect a right or interest in property`
            `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS `I acted to protect a right or privilege in or over land`
            `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `that right or interest was in fact vested in me or another`
            `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed that right or interest was vested in me or another`
            `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection`
            `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS `an honest belief if` `I honestly believed the means of protection were reasonable`
            `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS `I have another lawful excuse or defence recognised by law`
§ `Section 6 -- Search for things intended for use in committing offences of criminal damage`

-- s 6(1). The justice's power to grant a warrant is the person's LIABILITY: what can
-- be done to someone who has something in their custody, control or premises. The
-- judgments "made to appear" and "reasonable cause to believe" are the justice's, and
-- are taken as stated facts about the justice.
@export Can a justice of the peace grant a warrant to search for and seize something I have?
GIVEN `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has information on oath been laid before a justice of the peace?
      `there is reasonable cause to believe that I have the thing in my custody, under my control or on my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there reasonable cause to believe that you have the thing in your custody, under your control or on your premises?
      `there is reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used or is intended for use without lawful excuse to destroy or damage property belonging to another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used, or is intended for use, without lawful excuse to destroy or damage property belonging to another?
      `there is reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used or is intended for use without lawful excuse to destroy or damage property in a way likely to endanger the life of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used, or is intended for use, without lawful excuse to destroy or damage any property in a way likely to endanger the life of another?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a justice of the peace grant a warrant to search for and seize something I have` IS
    `a justice of the peace may grant a warrant authorising any constable to search for and seize the thing`
        `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace`
        `there is reasonable cause to believe that I have the thing in my custody, under my control or on my premises`
        `there is reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used or is intended for use without lawful excuse to destroy or damage property belonging to another`
        `there is reasonable cause to believe the thing has been used or is intended for use without lawful excuse to destroy or damage property in a way likely to endanger the life of another`

-- s 6(2). What an authorised constable may do on the person's premises.
@export Can a constable authorised by a warrant enter my premises, by force if need be, and search them?
GIVEN `the constable is authorised under section 6 to search my premises for the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the constable authorised, under a warrant granted under section 6, to search your premises for the thing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a constable authorised by a warrant enter my premises and search them` IS
    `the constable may enter the premises, by force if need be, and search them` `the constable is authorised under section 6 to search my premises for the thing`

@export Can the constable seize this thing from me?
GIVEN `the constable is authorised under section 6 to search my premises for something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the constable authorised, under a warrant granted under section 6, to search your premises for something?
      `the constable believes the thing has been used or is intended to be used as described in section 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the constable believe the thing has been used, or is intended to be used, to destroy or damage property as section 6(1) describes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the constable seize this thing from me` IS
    `the constable may seize the thing` `the constable is authorised under section 6 to search my premises for something` `the constable believes the thing has been used or is intended to be used as described in section 6(1)`

-- s 6(3). What happens afterwards to what the police have taken.
@export What law decides what happens to what the police have taken from me?
GIVEN `the property has come into the possession of the police under section 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the property come into the possession of the police under a warrant granted under section 6?
GIVETH A `Law governing property that came into police possession under section 6`
DECIDE `What law decides what happens to what the police have taken from me` IS
    `the law governing property that has come into the possession of the police under section 6` `the property has come into the possession of the police under section 6`

§ `Section 7 -- Jurisdiction of magistrates' courts`

-- s 7(2). The person has no immunity against being tried in a magistrates' court
-- because a dispute over who owns the property is involved.
@export Can a magistrates' court try me despite a dispute over who owns the property?
GIVEN `a rule of law says magistrates' courts cannot try offences where a dispute of title to property is involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a rule of law that says magistrates' courts cannot try offences where a dispute of title to property is involved?
      `I am charged with an offence under this Act or another offence of destroying or damaging property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under the Criminal Damage Act 1971, or another offence of destroying or damaging property?
GIVETH A `Effect of a dispute of title on the jurisdiction of magistrates' courts`
DECIDE `Can a magistrates' court try me despite a dispute over who owns the property` IS
    `the effect of a rule of law about a dispute of title on the jurisdiction of magistrates' courts` `a rule of law says magistrates' courts cannot try offences where a dispute of title to property is involved` `I am charged with an offence under this Act or another offence of destroying or damaging property`

§ `Section 9 -- Evidence in connection with offences under this Act`

-- s 9, first part. The person's DUTY to answer or comply in qualifying civil proceedings
-- although it may incriminate them or their spouse or civil partner.
@export Must I answer a question or obey an order even though it may incriminate me or my spouse?
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of property, for the execution of a trust or for an account of property or dealings with property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property, for the execution of any trust or for an account of any property or dealings with property?
      `a question is put to me in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a question put to you in those proceedings?
      `an order is made against me in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made against you in those proceedings?
      `answering or complying may incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May answering or complying incriminate you, or your spouse or civil partner, of an offence under the Criminal Damage Act 1971?
GIVETH A `Whether section 9 excuses a person from answering or complying`
DECIDE `Must I answer a question or obey an order even though it may incriminate me or my spouse` IS
    `whether the person is excused from answering or complying`
        `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of property, for the execution of a trust or for an account of property or dealings with property`
        `a question is put to me in those proceedings`
        `an order is made against me in those proceedings`
        `answering or complying may incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act`

-- s 9, second part. The person's IMMUNITY: what they said in answering or complying
-- cannot be used against them (or, unless they married afterwards, their spouse or
-- civil partner) in proceedings for an offence under the Act.
@export Can what I said in answering or complying be used in evidence against me or my spouse?
GIVEN `my statement or admission was made in answering a question put, or complying with an order made, in such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement or admission made in answering a question put, or complying with an order made, in proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property, for the execution of any trust or for an account of any property or dealings with property?
      `it is offered in proceedings for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered in proceedings for an offence under the Criminal Damage Act 1971?
      `it is offered against` IS A `Against whom a statement or admission is offered` @desc Against whom is it offered?
      `my spouse or civil partner married me or became my civil partner after I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is offered against your spouse or civil partner, did you marry or become civil partners after the statement or admission was made?
GIVETH A `Admissibility under section 9`
DECIDE `Can what I said in answering or complying be used in evidence against me or my spouse` IS
    `the admissibility of the statement or admission`
        `my statement or admission was made in answering a question put, or complying with an order made, in such proceedings`
        `it is offered in proceedings for an offence under this Act`
        `it is offered against`
        `my spouse or civil partner married me or became my civil partner after I made it`

§ `Section 10 -- Interpretation`

-- s 10(1). Whether a thing is "property" within the Act.
@export Is the thing "property" within the Act?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `What the thing is` @desc What best describes the thing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the thing property within the Act` IS
    `a thing is property within section 10(1)` (`the thing described by` `what the thing is`)

-- s 10(2) to (4). Whether the property is treated as belonging to someone else.
@export Is the property treated as belonging to someone else?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `What the thing is` @desc What best describes the thing?
      `someone else has custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does anyone other than you have custody or control of it?
      `what interest someone else has in it` IS A `Interest in property` @desc What interest, if any, does anyone other than you have in it? An interest that is only equitable and arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest is a separate choice.
      `someone else has a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does anyone other than you have a charge on it?
      `someone else has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can anyone other than you enforce a trust to which it is subject?
      `someone else is the corporation sole whose property it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone other than you the corporation sole (an office-holder that is a legal person in its own right, such as a bishop) whose property it is, whether or not the office is vacant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the property treated as belonging to someone else` IS
    `property belonging to another` `my property`
    WHERE
        `another person's connection` MEANS Connection WITH
            `custody or control of it` IS `someone else has custody or control of it`
            `interest in it` IS `what interest someone else has in it`
            `a charge on it` IS `someone else has a charge on it`
            `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS `someone else has a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
            `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS `someone else is the corporation sole whose property it is`
        
        `my property` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
            `the thing` IS `the thing described by` `what the thing is`
            `the accused's connection with it` IS `a connection not asked about`  -- not asked: this rule does not read it
            `other persons' connections with it` IS LIST `another person's connection`

@export Is the property treated as belonging to me?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `What the thing is` @desc What best describes the thing?
      `I have custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have custody or control of it?
      `what interest I have in it` IS A `Interest in property` @desc What interest, if any, do you have in it? An interest that is only equitable and arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest is a separate choice.
      `I have a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a charge on it?
      `I have a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you enforce a trust to which it is subject?
      `I am the corporation sole whose property it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation sole (an office-holder that is a legal person in its own right, such as a bishop) whose property it is, whether or not the office is vacant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the property treated as belonging to me` IS
    `property belonging to the accused` `my property`
    WHERE
        `my connection` MEANS Connection WITH
            `custody or control of it` IS `I have custody or control of it`
            `interest in it` IS `what interest I have in it`
            `a charge on it` IS `I have a charge on it`
            `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS `I have a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject`
            `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS `I am the corporation sole whose property it is`
        
        `my property` MEANS `Property facts` WITH
            `the thing` IS `the thing described by` `what the thing is`
            `the accused's connection with it` IS `my connection`
            `other persons' connections with it` IS EMPTY  -- not asked: this rule does not read it

-- s 10(5). Whether what was done to a computer is "damage" within the Act.
@export Is what I did to the computer or storage medium "destruction or damage" within the Act?
GIVEN `I destroyed or damaged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you destroy or damage it?
      `I did so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains?
      `the change impaired the physical condition of the computer or storage medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that change impair the physical condition of the computer or storage medium?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I did to the computer or storage medium damage within the Act` IS
    `destruction or damage within the Act` `my damage`
    WHERE
        `my damage` MEANS Damage WITH
            `destruction or damage` IS `I destroyed or damaged it`
            `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS `I did so only by changing what a computer or computer storage medium contains`
            `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS `the change impaired the physical condition of the computer or storage medium`

§ `Section 11 -- Arson at common law, and repealed procedure`

-- s 11(1). Whether the common law offence of arson can still be charged for what the
-- person did on the day they did it.
@export Can I be charged with the common law offence of arson?
GIVEN `the day I did it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you do it?
GIVETH A `Status of the common law offence of arson`
DECIDE `Can I be charged with the common law offence of arson` IS
    `the status of the common law offence of arson` `the day I did it`

-- s 11(11). Whether an old enactment about procedure or the powers of a court, repealed by
-- section 11, still applies to an offence committed before the repeal took effect.
@export Do the old rules of procedure or jurisdiction still apply to what I did before the repeal?
GIVEN `the enactment relates to procedure or to the jurisdictional powers of a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the old enactment relate to procedure, or to the jurisdictional powers of a court?
      `the enactment is repealed by section 11 or by an order made under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the old enactment repealed by section 11 of the Criminal Damage Act 1971, or by an order made under it?
      `the offence was committed before the repeal takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence you are charged with committed before the repeal took effect?
GIVETH A `Effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction`
DECIDE `Do the old rules of procedure or jurisdiction still apply to what I did before the repeal` IS
    `the effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction`
        `the enactment relates to procedure or to the jurisdictional powers of a court`
        `the enactment is repealed by section 11 or by an order made under it`
        `the offence was committed before the repeal takes effect`

§ `Section 12 -- Short title and extent`

-- s 12(1). From when the Act applies at all.
@export Was the Act in force on the day I did it?
GIVEN `the day I did it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you do it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the Act in force on the day I did it` IS
    `the Act is in force on` `the day I did it`

-- s 12(3), (6) and the long title. Where the Act's provisions reach.
@export Does the Act's text reach the place where I did it?
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place @desc In which place was it done?
GIVETH A `Whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to a place`
DECIDE `Does the Act's text reach the place where I did it` IS
    `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` `the place`
